                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 21 at 8:27PM MST until October 22 at 2:30AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 230 AM MST /330 AM MDT/ Tonight.\n\n* At 827 PM MST /927 PM MDT/, a river gauge on the Little Colorado\nRiver near the Colorado River reported a rapid rise of 5 feet from\nthunderstorms earlier today. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to\n1 inch are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing\nor expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nnormally dry washes, urban areas, highways, streets and\nunderpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLittle Colorado River Navajo Tribal Park and Salt Trail Canyon.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nthe Colorado River near mile marker 62. State Route 64 near mile\nmarker 282...and between mile markers 285 and 286.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas and campgrounds...\nBlue Water Base Camp, Old Fish Camp Site and Above LCR Camp Site.\n\nThis includes the following swimming holes...\nBlue Water Base Camp.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nBekihatso Wash, Colorado River, Little Colorado River, Moenkopi\nWash and Sheep Wash.",
                "instruction": "Flooding of washes and creeks will occur, some dirt roads will become\nmuddy and impassable. Paved roads and underpasses could become\nflooded as well.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
