                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 21 at 4:31PM MST until October 21 at 10:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Moenkopi Wash in...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 1000 PM MST /1100 PM MDT/.\n\n* At 431 PM MST /531 PM MDT/, a river gauge on the Moenkopi Wash\nremains in Major Flood Stage. Up to 1 inch of rain has fallen.\nAdditional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are possible in the\nwarned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Moenkopi Wash.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nMoenkopi Wash.\n\n* For Moenkopi Wash at Moenkopi Wash Near Tuba City:\nAt 1:45pm MST /2:45pm MDT/ the stage was 31.82 feet.\nFlood Stage is 27.0 feet.\nForecast: A crest of 30.97 feet is expected at 3:00pm MST /4:00pm\nMDT/ Wednesday.\nImpacts:\nAt 27.0 feet: At 27.0 feet water begins to encroach on homes in\nlower Moenkopi Village and floods crop fields along the river.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nTuba City and Moenkopi.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nHighway 160 between mile markers 318 and 321. U.S. Highway 89 between\nmile markers 476 and 478. State Route 264 between mile markers 323\nand 324.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nMoenkopi Wash, Little Colorado River, Hamblin Wash, Begashibito\nWash and Fivemile Wash.",
                "instruction": "This is a life threatening situation. Heavy rainfall will cause\nextensive and severe flash flooding of creeks...streams...and ditches\nin the Moenkopi Wash. Severe debris flows can also be anticipated\nacross roads. Roads and driveways may be washed away in places. If\nyou encounter flood waters...climb to safety.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
